  <!-- El Farol multi-seed replication.
       Purpose: the calibrated model shows El Farol's ToU effect collapsing to
       ~0 and the sf300 alternate-day oscillation disappearing. Both findings
       rest on a single seed, so this varies the seed at the baseline
       threshold (0.6) to check they are demand-driven, not seed-specific.

       IMPORTANT: `setup` runs `random-seed current-seed` whenever
       control-seed? is on (it is, seed 11), so raising `repetitions` does NOT
       vary the seed - every repetition is bit-identical (verified headless).
       Seeds must be varied through this enumeratedValueSet. Seed 11 is kept
       first so one cell reproduces the existing sensitivity-elfarol result. -->
  <experiment name="elfarol-seeds" repetitions="1" runMetricsEveryStep="true">
    <setup>setup</setup>
    <go>go-days</go>
    <exitCondition>current-sim-day &gt;= n-sim-days</exitCondition>
